Abstract
An n-divisor setis a finite set of positive integers containing a multiple of every integer
from 1 through n. Umans and Wang proposed, as the arithmetic-progression version of
their Strong ( α, β)-Divisor Conjecture, an n-divisor arithmetic progression having at most
n2β terms, each of magnitude at most exp(nα). We prove unconditionally that an n-divisor
arithmetic progression of heightHwith logH=o( √n) must have length
